			<title type="html"><![CDATA[Angela Nissel faces down grief with a laugh]]></title>
			<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.theverge.com/report/974226/angela-nissel-interview-good-grief-pass-the-bread-mom-is-dead" />
			<id>https://www.theverge.com/?p=974226</id>
			<updated>2026-08-01T16:13:56-04:00</updated>
			<published>2026-08-01T16:15:00-04:00</published>
			<category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Books" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Culture" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Entertainment" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Interview" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Report" />
							<summary type="html"><![CDATA[Angela Nissel's latest book, Good Grief, Pass the Bread, Mom Is Dead, is my kind of memoir. Sure, it's a deeply emotional tale about caring for a terminally ill parent. But it's delivered with the sort of gallows humor that I often turn to to get me through tough times. Of course, that sort of [&#8230;]]]></summary>
			
							<content type="html">
											<![CDATA[

						
<figure>

<img alt="Angela Nissel" data-caption="Angela Nissel smiles through the pain. | Image: Angela Nissel" data-portal-copyright="Image: Angela Nissel" data-has-syndication-rights="1" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/Angela-Nissel_Author-Headshot.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100" />
	<figcaption>
	Angela Nissel smiles through the pain. | Image: Angela Nissel	</figcaption>
</figure>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Angela Nissel's latest book, <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/0063345110?lv=shuf&amp;channelId=500&amp;plpRedirect=mhFallback"><em>Good Grief, Pass the Bread, Mom Is Dead</em></a><em>, </em>is my kind of memoir. Sure, it's a deeply emotional tale about caring for a terminally ill parent. But it's delivered with the sort of gallows humor that I often turn to to get me through tough times. </p>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Of course, that sort of dark humor should come as no surprise from Nissel. She first made a splash with <a href="https://www.amazon.com/Broke-Diaries-Completely-Hilarious-Misadventures/dp/0679783571/ref=pd_lpo_d_sccl_2/147-6007463-8645753?pd_rd_w=CWait&amp;content-id=amzn1.sym.4c8c52db-06f8-4e42-8e56-912796f2ea6c&amp;pf_rd_p=4c8c52db-06f8-4e42-8e56-912796f2ea6c&amp;pf_rd_r=774AS2NSH8H4533PAGJK&amp;pd_rd_wg=fzM79&amp;pd_rd_r=9e261540-4291-47ee-aef2-c0466f6b286c&amp;pd_rd_i=0679783571&amp;psc=1"><em>The Broke Diaries</em></a>, which grew out of a blog she kept in college detailing her daily struggles and, at times, embarrassment at being a broke student. Eventually she went on to produce and write for hit shows including <a href="https://www.hulu.com/series/bba197b5-eb03-4a09-b5f6-f04c053471d7"><em>Scrubs</em></a> and <a href="https://www.hbomax.com/shows/boondocks/c43c65e7-49fe-4795-9e13-759bad094a78?utm_source=universal_search"><em>The Boondocks</em></a>.</p>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One of her most lasting cont …</p>
<p><a href="https://www.theverge.com/report/974226/angela-nissel-interview-good-grief-pass-the-bread-mom-is-dead">Read the full story at The Verge.</a></p>
						]]>
									</content>
			
					</entry>
