			<title type="html"><![CDATA[Is this Billboard Hot 100 hit AI slop?]]></title>
			<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/974209/fenix-flexin-billboard-hot-100-rubberz-ai-slop" />
			<id>https://www.theverge.com/?p=974209</id>
			<updated>2026-08-01T14:18:49-04:00</updated>
			<published>2026-08-01T14:20:00-04:00</published>
			<category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="AI" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Entertainment" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Music" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Report" />
							<summary type="html"><![CDATA[Fenix Flexin is best known as a member of Shoreline Mafia, a rap duo from Los Angeles. But he's recently found solo success with the track "Rubberz," which has climbed to number 58 on the Billboard Hot 100. Almost immediately, though, questions were raised about the song's origins, with many speculating that it was largely, [&#8230;]]]></summary>
			
							<content type="html">
											<![CDATA[

						
<figure>

<img alt="The seemingly AI generated cover art for Fenix Flexin’s Rubberz." data-caption="That cover art is almost certainly AI, too. | Image: Fenix Flexin" data-portal-copyright="Image: Fenix Flexin" data-has-syndication-rights="1" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/artworks-WsdIgVXV8NOV-0-t1080x1080.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100" />
	<figcaption>
	That cover art is almost certainly AI, too. | Image: Fenix Flexin	</figcaption>
</figure>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fenix Flexin is best known as a member of Shoreline Mafia, a rap duo from Los Angeles. But he's recently found solo success with the track "<a href="https://youtu.be/Hl5_Lc6b3AU">Rubberz</a>," which has climbed to number 58 on the <a href="https://www.billboard.com/charts/hot-100/">Billboard Hot 100</a>. Almost immediately, though, questions were raised about the song's origins, with many speculating that it was largely, if not <a href="https://youtu.be/fzkoENoDrbs">entirely</a>, generated by AI. Fenix has denied those accusations, but done little to dispel them.</p>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Part of the suspicion is certainly due to the fact that the song is a dramatic left turn. Fenix has primarily trafficked in <a href="https://youtu.be/Ib-tOtLDdRA">trap-influenced</a> <a href="https://youtu.be/17TthjWbvVY">West Coast</a> <a href="https://youtu.be/0wsCBQlB79k">rap</a>. "Rubberz," on the other hand, is heavily influenced by '80s UK s …</p>
<p><a href="https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/974209/fenix-flexin-billboard-hot-100-rubberz-ai-slop">Read the full story at The Verge.</a></p>
						]]>
									</content>
			
					</entry>
