			<title type="html"><![CDATA[With Switch 2, iPhone, and laptop tricks, the Sharge Disk Pro 2 is finally a worthy EDC]]></title>
			<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/973886/sharge-disk-pro-2-hands-on-switch-2-hdmi-usb-c-dock" />
			<id>https://www.theverge.com/?p=973886</id>
			<updated>2026-07-31T19:11:42-04:00</updated>
			<published>2026-07-31T18:09:11-04:00</published>
			<category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Gadgets" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Hands-on" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Reviews" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Tech" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="USB-C" />
							<summary type="html"><![CDATA[Sharge, the company that makes delightful retro Mac-shaped chargers and see-inside batteries, is finally impressing me with a portable SSD. I couldn't recommend the Sharge Disk, Disk Plus, or even the Disk Pro, but I'd be happy to own the new Disk Pro 2 Ultra. This isn't just a drive. It's a 4K HDMI dock [&#8230;]]]></summary>
			
							<content type="html">
											<![CDATA[

						
<figure>

<img alt="A playing-card-deck-sized gadget with a transparent front, showing off computer chips and a fan and an SSD inside, as well as a detachable yellow USB-C cable shaped into a lanyard." data-caption="The Sharge Disk Pro 2. | Photo by Sean Hollister / The Verge" data-portal-copyright="Photo by Sean Hollister / The Verge" data-has-syndication-rights="1" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/07/verge-sharge-disk-pro-2-sean-hollister-1.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100" />
	<figcaption>
	The Sharge Disk Pro 2. | Photo by Sean Hollister / The Verge	</figcaption>
</figure>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sharge, the company that makes <a href="https://www.theverge.com/2024/2/7/24065111/sharge-retro67-usbc-charger-mac">delightful retro Mac-shaped chargers</a> and <a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/876432/sharge-shargeek-300w-power-bank-rgb-lighting-kickstarter">see-inside batteries</a>, is finally impressing me with a portable SSD. I couldn't recommend the Sharge Disk, Disk Plus, or even the Disk Pro, but I'd be happy to own <a href="https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/shargetech/disk-pro-2">the new Disk Pro 2 Ultra</a>.</p>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This isn't just a drive. It's a 4K HDMI dock and a USB-C hub too. It's a veritable USB-C Swiss Army Knife for all your main gadgets: laptop, tablet, phone, Steam Deck, even the Nintendo Switch and Switch 2. </p>
<div class="youtube-embed"><iframe title="One tiny dock to rule them all? #TITW" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/lvz_9pTFmq4?rel=0" allowfullscreen allow="accelerometer *; clipboard-write *; encrypted-media *; gyroscope *; picture-in-picture *; web-share *;"></iframe></div>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And this USB multitool has built-in MagSafe pattern magnets to stick it to your iPhone, Pixel, or anything where you're willing to stick a magnetic ring. (One stick-on ring is in …</p>
<p><a href="https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/973886/sharge-disk-pro-2-hands-on-switch-2-hdmi-usb-c-dock">Read the full story at The Verge.</a></p>
						]]>
